---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy | GurtOS at Cal Hacks 13.0" description="What the GurtOS Cal Hacks showcase site collects: nothing of its own. A plain account of what the host and linked services may see.">
  <article class="wrap legal">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>What this site collects</h1>
    <p class="lead">This is a static showcase for a hackathon project. It has no accounts, no forms, no comments and no cookies of its own, and it adds no analytics or tracking code. We collect nothing from you.</p>

    <h2>What the host sees</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel receives each request to show you a page (your IP address,
      your browser's user agent and the page you asked for) and may keep ordinary server logs and, if it is switched on
      for the project, cookie-free page-view counts. Vercel's own privacy notice governs that. We do not read or
      export those logs for anything but keeping the site running.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not set cookies, store anything in your browser, or fingerprint it.</li>
      <li>We do not run third-party scripts, ads or trackers.</li>
      <li>We do not ask for your name, email or any personal detail, and we do not sell or share data, because we hold none.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Videos and links</h2>
    <p>
      The video clips on this site are files served from the site itself. If a narrated video is added later, it loads
      from YouTube's privacy-enhanced domain only when the page is opened. Links to GitHub, Mana, Agentverse, Figma,
      Solana Explorer and other sites take you to services with their own privacy notices. Downloads of the install
      discs come from GitHub Releases and a Vultr Object Storage mirror, which see the download request.
    </p>

    <h2>The software</h2>
    <p>
      GurtOS is software you run on your own computer. This site does not collect any data from a GurtOS box, and a box
      sends nothing to us. Each box's own docs say what it stores and where.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>To ask about this page, open an issue in the project's <a href={LINKS.repo}>GitHub repository</a>.</p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated Oct 24, 2026.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .legal .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-focus);
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 1.3em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }
  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
